As it turns out, if you did diskutil list, you will find that the Recovery Disk comes as part of the Installation.

Reboot and press the Command and "S" keys down and you will enter the shell which is already at root.

[a] If you want to restart the Installation process for update again (say you lost root passwd or got stripped of admin rights for some reason)
    in this mode, just delete /var/db/.AppleSetupDone and reboot

